==Parameters== <!--T:5-->

<!--T:6-->
The macro presents a dialog with the following parameters:

* **Width** (default: 100 mm): Inner width of the box along the X-axis
* **Depth** (default: 100 mm): Inner depth of the box along the Y-axis
* **Height** (default: 100 mm): Inner height of the box along the Z-axis
* **Thickness** (default: 4 mm): Material thickness — this determines the depth of the notches
* **Notch Width** (default: 20 mm): Width of each interlocking finger/notch
* **Clearance** (default: 0.2 mm): Extra space between interlocking parts for a comfortable fit. Typical laser cutting clearance: 0.1–0.3 mm
* **Notch Type** (default: Square): Shape of the notches — Square or Rounded
* **Export DXF** (checkbox): Automatically exports the generated faces as DXF files for laser cutting

==Usage== <!--T:7-->

<!--T:8-->
# Run the macro from {{MenuCommand|Macro → Macros → Macro BoxCreator → Execute}}
# A dialog will appear with the parameter fields described above
# Adjust the parameters to match your desired box dimensions and material thickness
# Click **OK** to generate the box
# The following objects will be created in the document tree:
#* **BoxCreator_Front** and **BoxCreator_Back**
#* **BoxCreator_Left** and **BoxCreator_Right**
#* **BoxCreator_Top** and **BoxCreator_Bottom**
# Each part has interlocking notches and can be selected individually for further operations

==Notes== <!--T:9-->

<!--T:10-->
* The total outer dimensions will be {{incode|Width + 2*Thickness}} by {{incode|Depth + 2*Thickness}} by {{incode|Height + Thickness}}
* Notch width should typically be between 10-30 mm for most box sizes
* Clearance should be adjusted based on your material and cutting method:
** Laser cutting: 0.1-0.3 mm
** 3D printing: 0.2-0.5 mm
** CNC routing: 0.3-0.6 mm
* The macro works in millimeters; convert units before running if using imperial

